  "worked_solution": "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/16408e6add22c687e3d2cf865908011602bfa87878fcbc3387c4ad3d22180e47.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<arg\u2061(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan\u2061(\\frac{11}{8})=0.942\\,000\u2026\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg\u2061(z)=2\\pi -0.942\\,000\u22485.34,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
